    "body": "@domenic, I am referring to <iframe> element.\r\n\r\nI think Chrome [Issue #365457](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=365457), [Issue #899559](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=899559) and [Issue #938279](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=938279), and likely other browsers are missing this part \r\n\r\n> https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/iframe-embed-object.html\r\n> If the load failed (e.g. there was an HTTP 404 error, there was a DNS error), fire an event named error at the element, then jump to the step below labeled fallback.\r\n\r\nChrome doesn't fire error event and instead fires load event when iframe load failed by CSP or other reason.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
